course: dictionary
lesson: 15533
title: Suggestive: hints and clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something is suggestive of something else, it makes you think of that thing or hints at it. «The grey clouds are suggestive of rain.» The clouds do not say it will rain, but they make you think it may come soon.
explain: Suggestive can also mean giving a clue or sign that something may be true. «The muddy boots by the door were suggestive: someone had been in the garden.» The boots do not prove it, but they point the way. Ask yourself: what does this hint at?
explain: Scientists use the word carefully too. «The results are suggestive but not certain» means the evidence points one way, but it is not proof yet.
fact: Suggestive means hinting at something, or making you think of it.
fact: «Suggestive of» is a common phrase: «The smell in the kitchen was suggestive of baking bread.»
fact: «Highly suggestive» means a very strong hint, though it may still not be proof.
fact: In stories and art, a suggestive picture or sound brings an idea to mind without saying it outright.
fact: A suggestive clue points towards an answer, but it is weaker than proof.
exercise: «The dark sky was suggestive of a storm coming.» What does suggestive mean here? | *Hinting at a storm | Very loud and angry | Blue and bright | Proving there is a storm for certain
exercise: «The results are suggestive but not certain.» What does suggestive mean in this sentence? | Funny and silly | *Pointing towards something, but not proof | Old and dusty | Proof of something for sure
exercise: Which phrase means it makes you think of something? | *suggestive of | suggested for | suggestive as | suggests nothing
test: «The sound of waves was suggestive of the sea, even in the city.» What does suggestive mean? | A kind of boat | Very cold and wet | *Making you think of the sea | Making the sea disappear
test: «The muddy boots were highly suggestive.» What do the boots hint at? | The boots are for swimming | Nobody has been outside | *Someone has been outside | The boots are brand new
exam: Ruby says «The paint on the wall was suggestive of a sunset.» What does this tell you? | The wall was a window | Ruby painted the sunset herself | The paint was a real sunset | *The paint made you think of a sunset
